course: dictionary
lesson: 14806
title: Purely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Purely» is an adverb. It tells you how or why something happens. Its most common meaning is only, or for no other reason. «I did it purely for fun.» Nobody asked me to, and there was no other reason: I did it because it was fun.
explain: «Purely» can also mean completely or entirely. «The story is a purely made-up tale» means every part of it was invented. To choose the right meaning, look at the words around it. If the sentence gives a reason, think only. If it describes how much, think completely.
explain: «Purely» can also mean in a clean way, with nothing mixed in. «The lab test showed the liquid was purely water.» Look for phrases like purely by chance, purely an accident and purely and simply. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Purely is an adverb, so it tells you how or why something happens.
fact: «Purely» means only, simply, or for no other reason: «I did it purely for fun.»
fact: «Purely» can mean completely or entirely: «a purely made-up story».
fact: «Purely» can mean with nothing mixed in: «The liquid was purely water.»
fact: Common phrases: purely by chance, purely an accident, purely and simply.
exercise: «We went to the park purely to see the ducks.» What does purely mean here? | Completely wet | Loudly | *Only, for no other reason | Very fast
exercise: «She won the prize purely by chance.» What does purely mean here? | Slowly and carefully | *Only, with no other reason behind it | Completely, from start to end | Very happily
exercise: «The story is purely made-up, so none of it is true.» What does purely mean in this sentence? | *Completely, from start to end | Sadly | Quietly | Partly, a little bit
test: «I bought the bike purely because it was cheap.» Why did they buy the bike? | Because it was red | *Only because it was cheap, for no other reason | Because a friend asked them to
test: «The lab tested the sample and found it was purely water.» What does purely mean here? | Very hot | Only a little bit wet | Quickly poured | *With nothing mixed in
exam: «Ben was late purely by accident.» What does purely by accident mean? | Ben was late on purpose | He was late because of the rain | *It happened only by accident, with no other reason | He planned it carefully
